    <briefdescription>
<para>Struct template representing the absolute value of the minimum of a signed integral type, as written in a literal. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The signed integral type of the literal.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The absolute value of the minimum of a signed type (e.g. 128 for <computeroutput>int8_t</computeroutput>) does not fit in the type, but the literal must be accepted to write the minimum with the unary minus (e.g. <computeroutput>-128<ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-literals_1ga265f8609ef3d6ead78c7a66825553e24" kindref="member">_i8</ref></computeroutput>). The literal operators return this type for such a literal; its only operation is the unary minus, so any other use of the literal fails to compile. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
